# Data File Editing Rules

## Schema Constraints

Each YAML file has a specific schema. When editing, preserve the structure.

### itinerary.yaml
```yaml
cities:
  - name: "City Name"
    jp: "日本語"           # Japanese characters for the city
    flag: "🏯"             # Single emoji
    dates: "Oct X – Y"
    nights: "N nights"
    days:
      - num: "DAY N"
        date: "Oct X"
        title: "Day title"
        places:
          - tag: "main|quiet|food"    # CSS class for styling
            tag_text: "Morning"       # Display label
            name: "Place Name"
            desc: "Description text"
```

### hidden-gems.yaml
```yaml
gems:
  - city: "City Name"
    name: "Place Name"
    description: "Why it's special"
    crowd_level: 1          # 1-5, controls filled dots
    crowd_label: "Very Low" # Very Low, Low, Moderate, High, Very High
```

### budget.yaml
- `weight` is a 0-1 float controlling bar width (1.0 = full bar)
- Recalculate weights relative to the highest item when adding new entries

### checklist.yaml
- Items are plain strings in arrays under group titles
- Keep groups to 4-7 items for readability

## Validation
- All YAML must be valid — use proper quoting for strings with colons or special chars
- Emoji should be used sparingly in `desc` fields
- Japanese text (`jp` fields) should use proper kanji/hiragana
